    "blurb": "NinMed is reconstructing and translating the world’s most standardised, structured and systematised corpus of medical literature prior to Galen: the “Nineveh Medical Encyclopaedia” from the library of Ashurbanipal, King of Assyria (669-c.630 BC).  Funded by the Wellcome Trust. Directed by Jon Taylor in collaboration with Mark Geller, and with the assistance of Irving Finkel.    ",
